    "DisplayName": "Cumulonimbus",
    "Notes": "A tower to nine kilometres plus the ANVIL, a second lobe at 9.5 km that no single-humped curve can produce and the profile table can. The anvil is what makes the type recognisable from the ground. Placement scale 2.00: a storm cell is tens of kilometres across and there is ONE of it, not a field. At the shipped 12 km layer tile this puts a 6 km cell under a 9 km tower, which is the aspect a real cumulonimbus has.",
